  "definition": "Thalidomide is a drug that inhibits tumor necrosis factor alpha (TNFα) and has anti-inflammatory, anti-angiogenic, and anti-tumor effects. In the supplied source, it is discussed as a possible way to reduce Alzheimer-like brain changes and related learning and memory deficits in a mouse model when given over a long period.",
